WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
Morning, afternoon and evening: Jewish
prayer has three set times every day.

2
00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:10.320
At the heart of every service
is one prayer: the Amidah.

3
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:14.190
It is said standing, feet
together, facing Jerusalem.

4
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.280
And it is said in silence.

5
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.090
Only the lips move.

6
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.950
So why do Jews stand so
still for one silent prayer,

7
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.160
three times every day?

8
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.140
In this mission, you'll follow
a Shabbat morning service,

9
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:28.610
step by step.

10
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.580
Then you'll compare Orthodox
and Reform services,

11
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.770
from language to who leads.

12
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:37.300
Your mission: find out
why Jews pray this way,

13
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.390
standing still and silent.
